From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: name the pin banks' I/O supplies

Seven pin banks logged a dummy regulator and "Couldn't set bank P? I/O
bias: -22" on every boot. A bank without a vcc-pX-supply property gets the
dummy regulator, whose voltage cannot be read, so the pin driver cannot set
the bank's withstand mode and says so. Name the supplies from the schematic
(V1.10):

  PB    VCC-IO, SWOUT2. PB has no POW_MOD_SEL field of its own, so the
        driver leaves it alone; the property only replaces the dummy.
  PC    VCC-PC, CLDO5 at 1.8 V. The eMMC consumes the same rail as vqmmc.
  PD    VCC33-LCD, SWOUT1, through R251 (0R). BLDO2 carries a VCC-PD label
        but its output does not reach the SoC ball.
  PE PK BLDO1, which also feeds VCC-MCSI.
  PF    VCC-IO (SWOUT2) or VCC18-PF (CLDO5), selected by the power-source
        of its pin groups; it names VCC-IO, the selection after reset. The
        withstand mode of PF follows the switch, not this property.
  PG    VCC-PG is tied to VCC-PL through RA3: ALDO1.
  PH    VCC-PH, SWOUT2. Without the phandle the bank finds the rail by its
        regulator-name, without a log line and only if it is registered by
        then, so GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL came up in the adaptive mode in some boots
        and in the 3.3 V mode in others. With it a rail that is not there yet
        defers gmac0, and the mode is the same in every boot.
  PJ    VCC33-LCD, SWOUT1, no series part.
  PM    (r_pio) The VCC-PM ball reaches VCC-PL (ALDO1) through RA13 (0R).
        The net named VCC-PM on CLDO1 does not reach the SoC, a CLDO1
        phandle would write the 1.8 V mode onto a 3.3 V bank.

Add ALDO1 as vcc-pl-pg-pm and BLDO1 as vcc-pe-pk-mcsi, both always on and
without a voltage window like the other rails of the PMIC: ALDO1 feeds bank
PL, which the PMIC's own I2C bus runs on, and nothing consumes VCC-MCSI, so
the regulator core would switch BLDO1 off after boot. ALDO1 is not called
vcc-pl: a bank without a phandle looks a rail up by the name of its supply,
and bank PL has none.

Bank PL stays without a supply. Its consumer is r_i2c0 (PL0/PL1), the bus
the PMIC sits on, and it requests its pins before the PMIC exists, so a
vcc-pl-supply from ALDO1 would defer the controller that has to probe first
for ALDO1 to exist. It keeps the dummy regulator and its two log lines.

The A733 r-pinctrl has its own driver, so the comment on the r_pio node
that described the A523 driver's one-bit write is replaced.

This replaces `arm64-dts-a733-bank-pc-io-supply` and
`arm64-dts-a733-bank-ph-io-supply`, which named PC and PH; this patch names
the remaining banks from the schematic.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -671,6 +671,52 @@ pio: pinctrl@2000000 {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 
+			/*
+			 * Pin bank supplies. The pin driver puts each bank's withstand
+			 * mode where its supply voltage says (two-bit GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL,
+			 * UM V1.00 18.14.6.1), and a bank without a supply property takes
+			 * the dummy regulator and logs it. Rails per the schematic V1.10:
+			 *
+			 *  - PB: VCC-IO, SWOUT2. PB has no field of its own: the UM names
+			 *    bits 25:24 VCCIO_PWR_MOD_SEL without tying them to a bank,
+			 *    and a733_io_bias_field_shift[] marks PB NO_FIELD. The
+			 *    property only replaces the dummy regulator, no register is
+			 *    written.
+			 *  - PC: VCC-PC, CLDO5, 1.8 V (the eMMC consumes the same rail as
+			 *    vqmmc).
+			 *  - PD: VCC33-LCD, SWOUT1: ball 1N7 reaches it through R251
+			 *    (0R), not through BLDO2, whose output only carries a VCC-PD
+			 *    label.
+			 *  - PE, PK: BLDO1, which also feeds VCC-MCSI.
+			 *  - PF: VCC-IO (SWOUT2) or VCC18-PF (CLDO5), selected by the
+			 *    power-source of its pin groups. The property names VCC-IO,
+			 *    the selection after reset. The withstand mode of PF is not
+			 *    written from it, it follows the switch (NO_FIELD).
+			 *  - PG: VCC-PG is tied to VCC-PL through RA3, ALDO1.
+			 *  - PH: VCC-PH, SWOUT2, 3.3 V. Without the phandle the bank
+			 *    still finds a rail named "vcc-ph", but only if it is
+			 *    registered by then, without a log line, and GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL
+			 *    15:14 came up 01 (adaptive) in some boots and 10 (3.3 V) in
+			 *    others. With the phandle a rail that is not there yet defers
+			 *    the consumer (gmac0) and the mode is the same in every boot.
+			 *  - PJ: VCC33-LCD, SWOUT1, no series part.
+			 *
+			 * Bank PL has no supply here: its consumer is r_i2c0 (PL0/PL1),
+			 * the bus the PMIC itself sits on, and it requests its pins before
+			 * the PMIC exists. A vcc-pl-supply from ALDO1 would defer the I2C
+			 * controller that has to probe first for ALDO1 to exist. Bank PM,
+			 * on r_pio, runs from the same rail and gets its supply there.
+			 */
+			vcc-pb-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+			vcc-pc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
+			vcc-pd-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
+			vcc-pe-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
+			vcc-pf-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+			vcc-pg-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+			vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+			vcc-pj-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
+			vcc-pk-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
+
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
@@ -2295,13 +2341,10 @@ gmac0_syscon: syscon@4508000 {
 		 * (root interrupt-parent). We use only PM5 as a GPIO output (VBUS
 		 * enable); the EINT domain is set up but unused.
 		 *
-		 * Caveat: the a523-r driver sets io_bias_cfg_variant =
-		 * BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL, the 1-bit write that does not fit
-		 * the A733's 2-bit POW_MOD_SEL. It stays dormant here because
-		 * no bank has a vcc-pX-supply: the dummy regulator has no ops and no
-		 * fixed_uV, so regulator_get_voltage() returns -EINVAL and set_io_bias
-		 * leaves at its uV < 0 branch. A PL/PM supply needs an A733 r-pinctrl
-		 * carrying the correct 2-bit variant -- that is `pinctrl-sunxi-add-a733-r-pinctrl`.
+		 * The A733 has its own r-pinctrl driver with the two-bit
+		 * SGPIO_POW_MOD_SEL (PL at 1:0, PM at 3:2). Bank PM carries a
+		 * supply (vcc-pm-supply on r_pio), bank PL none, see the pin bank
+		 * supplies on pio.
 		 */
 		r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu";
@@ -2377,6 +2420,15 @@ r_pio: pinctrl@7025000 {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 
+			/*
+			 * Bank PM: the VCC-PM ball reaches VCC-PL, ALDO1, 3.3 V, through
+			 * RA13 (0R); the net named VCC-PM on CLDO1 does not reach the
+			 * SoC. SGPIO_POW_MOD_SEL 3:2 gets 10 (3.3 V mode) from it, the
+			 * reset value. No vcc-pl-supply: see the pin bank supplies on
+			 * pio.
+			 */
+			vcc-pm-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+
 			/*
 			 * PMU I2C = S_TWI0 on PL0/PL1 (mux 2). Pin/mux from the
 			 * pin tables (PL0 = S-TWI0-SCK, PL1 = S-TWI0-SDA)
@@ -2574,6 +2626,27 @@ reg_dcdc5: dcdc5 {
 						regulator-always-on;
 					};
 
+					/*
+					 * VCC-PL: bank PL (the PMIC bus pins), banks PG and PM, the
+					 * EEPROM and the TWI0 pull-ups. Always on: the PMIC bus runs
+					 * on bank PL. 3.3 V as read back from the PMIC, no window.
+					 * Not "vcc-pl": a bank finds a rail by that name, PL has none.
+					 */
+					reg_aldo1: aldo1 {
+						regulator-name = "vcc-pl-pg-pm";
+						regulator-always-on;
+					};
+
+					/*
+					 * 1.8 V I/O: banks PE and PK, VCC-MCSI and the camera
+					 * signals on J5. Always on: VCC-MCSI names no supply, so the
+					 * regulator core would switch the rail off after boot.
+					 */
+					reg_bldo1: bldo1 {
+						regulator-name = "vcc-pe-pk-mcsi";
+						regulator-always-on;
+					};
+
 					/*
 					 * SWOUT1 = reg 0x11 BIT(3) = Maxio PHY
 					 * 3v3 (board net VCC33-LCD). SWOUT2 =
